Subject: [PATCH] [M159] SchemeHostPort: Reject empty host for non-file
 SCHEME_WITH_HOST schemes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

FlyWeb port (not yet merged to M156): from branch-heads/8154 b079c8f6c8 (M159 merge of 73392c2e5d). Applied after portes-159/chromium/0001; applies cleanly (identical diff). No brave-core patches or chromium_src for url/.

Original change's description:
> SchemeHostPort: Reject empty host for non-file SCHEME_WITH_HOST schemes
>
> Before this CL, a `url::SchemeHostPort` could have an empty host for
> *any* `SCHEME_WITH_HOST` scheme, e.g. `("chrome", "", 0)`.  But among
> such schemes, only `file:` `GURL`s may actually have an empty host -
> `GURL` rejects "chrome://" [1] and other similar URLs with "standard"
> schemes [2].  Therefore such a `SchemeHostPort` couldn't originate from
> a `GURL`.  Nevertheless, when such an empty-host `SchemeHostPort` was
> received via IPC, it could confuse the navigation stack.
>
> After this CL, `SchemeHostPort` (and therefore also `url::Origin`,
> including its mojo traits) treats an empty host as invalid for
> `SCHEME_WITH_HOST` schemes other than `file:` (just like `GURL` does).
> This also matches Blink, which derives origins from `KURL`s, and where
> "chrome://" and other similar URLs are invalid and result in opaque
> origins [3].
>
> [1] `SchemeHostPortTest.EmptyHostGurlConversion` registers "chrome" as
>     a `SCHEME_WITH_HOST` scheme, and checks that `GURL("chrome:")` and
>     `GURL("chrome://")` (the serialization of `("chrome", "", 0)`) are
>     invalid (note that this CL tweaks this test slightly - the link
>     points to the state before this CL):
>     https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/989bfb21678bad41c86612a54df922726246ecd7:url/scheme_host_port_unittest.cc;l=290-299
> [2] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/989bfb21678bad41c86612a54df922726246ecd7:url/url_canon_stdurl.cc;l=76-84
> [3] `AbstractOriginTest.OpaqueOriginsFromInvalidUrls` checks that URLs
>     of `SCHEME_WITH_HOST` schemes without a host are invalid and result
>     in opaque origins:
>     https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/989bfb21678bad41c86612a54df922726246ecd7:url/origin_abstract_tests.h;l=385-400
>     Blink runs this test with `KURL` and `blink::SecurityOrigin`:
>     https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/989bfb21678bad41c86612a54df922726246ecd7:third_party/blink/renderer/platform/weborigin/security_origin_test.cc;l=1364-1366
>
